,"lo":-123.847934,"d":174,"wp":"en:Astoria Victory Monument","wd":"Q4811119","ds":"The Astoria Victory Monument, also known as the Doughboy Monument or Soldiers' Monument, is a monument located in Astoria, Oregon, in the United States. It is listed on the National Register of Historic Places. The concrete, Spanish Revival monument designed by Charles T. Diamond was constructed in 1926, incorporating a cast of a sculpture by John Paulding.","wpu":"Astoria Victory Monument","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Doughboy_Monument_-_Astoria%2C_Oregon.jpg/960px-Doughboy_Monument_-_Astoria%2C_Oregon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Goonies \"Mouth's House\"","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":46.185978,"lo":-123.8424,"d":674,"ad":"32 Skyline Avenue"},{"n":"Windwater Bed & Breakfast Suite","g":"sights","k":"guest_house","la":46.188622,"lo":-123.841224,"d":676,"w":"https://windwaterbedandbreakfast.com/","ph":"+1 503-338-8702","wifi":1},{"n":"Astoria Riverfront Trolley","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":46.185853,"lo":-123.858894,"d":768,"h":"May Mo[4]-Sep Mo[1] 12:00-18:00","w":"https://old300.org/","ph":"+1 503 325-6311;+1 503 325-8790;+1 800 875-6807","ds":"The Astoria Riverfront Trolley is a 3-mile (4.8 km) heritage streetcar line that operates in Astoria, Oregon, United States, using former freight railroad tracks along or near the south bank of the Columbia River, with no overhead line. The service began operating in 1999, using a 1913-built streetcar from San Antonio, Texas.","wpu":"Astoria Riverfront Trolley","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Astoria_Riverfront_Trolley_-_Old_300_at_12th_Street.jpg/960px-Astoria_Riverfront_Trolley_-_Old_300_at_12th_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Douglas Fir","g":"sights","k":"attraction","la":46.188969,"lo":-123.835515,"d":1115},{"n":"Oregon Film Museum","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":46.188544,"lo":-123.835493,"d":1117,"h":"May-Sep 10:00-17:00; Oct-Apr 10:00-16:00","w":"https://astoriamuseums.org/explore/oregon-film-museum/","wp":"en:Oregon Film Museum","wd":"Q7101207","ad":"732 Duane Street","ds":"The Oregon Film Museum is a museum highlighting and celebrating movies that were made in the U.S. state of Oregon. The museum is housed in the old Clatsop County Jail in Astoria, Oregon, which is on the National Register of Historic Places. The building was used in the opening chase sequence of the 1985 film The Goonies.","wpu":"Oregon Film Museum","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Oregon_Film_Museum%2C_County_Jail%2C_Astoria.JPG/960px-Oregon_Film_Museum%2C_County_Jail%2C_Astoria.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Flavel House","g":"sights","k":"museum","la":46.188131,"lo":-123.83513,"d":1148,"w":"https://www.cumtux.org/default.asp?pageid=35","ph":"+1 503 3252203","wp":"en:George C. and Winona Flavel House","wd":"Q5036654","ad":"441 8th Street","ds":"The George C. and Winona Flavel House is a house built in 1879 in Astoria, Oregon. It was listed on the National Register of Historic Places in 1991. This was the residence of Captain George Conrad Flavel (1855–1923) and his wife Winona from 1879 to 1901.","wpu":"George C. and Winona Flavel House","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/George_C._and_Winona_Flavel_House_-_Astoria%2C_Oregon.jpg/960px-George_C._and_Winona_Flavel_House_-_Astoria%2C_Oregon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Kala@Hipfish Monthly","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":46.189602,"lo":-123.832432,"d":1353},{"n":"Salty Raven","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":46.189605,"lo":-123.832372,"d":1358},{"n":"Cambium Gallery","g":"sights","k":"gallery","la":46.18847,"lo":-123.832335,"d":1361,"w":"https://www.cambiumgallery.com/","ph":"+1 971-988-9054","ad":"1030 Duane Street"},{"n":"Lightbox","g":"sig